    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We take the convention 0 ∈ N. Let x := 1 + |x|2 be the Japanese bracket. By A k B we mean that there exists C > 0 (which depends on k) for every A,B, A ≤ CB. The Schwartz space is the Fre´chet space S of m-forms α such that for every N ∈ N, |α(x)| N x −N [H¨or15, §7.1]. A density argument shows that a compactly supported m-current is determined by its action on S ."
